\n\
The only downside is no land in hand, but Leyline of Resonance comes into play tapped, and I’m playing first. That means I can play Leyline on turn one, and assuming I have a Mountain in my next draw (or topdeck), I’ll be rolling on turn two.\n\
\n\
However, going first with no land on a 7-card hand is risky. But this hand is full of tempo and explosive potential. Leyline is free on turn one since I’m starting, and if I hit a Mountain soon, I can flood the board.\n\
\n\
Mulligan decisions: we’re built to play fast. If I mulligan to 6, I risk a worse land draw and less explosive power. This hand, while landless, is highly synergistic and explosive if I find a Mountain in the next few draws.\n\
\n\
Verdict: Keep.\n\
\n\
