    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "KimiK2 ESPN played Razorkin Needlehead before playing their land (Riverpyre Verge) for the turn. By playing the land first, they would have had 3 mana available, opening up more options like casting Hired Claw + having mana for Burst Lightning, or holding up Lightning Strike. Playing creatures before land is a sequencing error that reduces flexibility. Additionally, casting a creature before combat when holding combat tricks and having Burnout Bashtronaut that could attack is slightly suboptimal - though with only 2 Mountains the Needlehead costs both mana so there's no trick mana available anyway.",
